Project Testing Phase

ComicCraft-AI – Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

The Project Testing Phase is carried out after development to ensure that ComicCraft-AI works correctly, produces meaningful comic stories, and provides a smooth user experience. Different testing methods are used to identify and fix errors before the final deployment.

1. Testing Objectives

The main objectives are to:

Check whether all system features work correctly.

Verify the integration with Gemini models.

Ensure that user inputs are processed correctly.

Check the quality and relevance of generated stories.

Identify and fix software errors.

Verify that the application is easy to use.

Ensure that user projects are stored correctly.


2. Types of Testing

Testing Type	Purpose

Unit Testing	Tests individual modules such as story generation and character creation.
Integration Testing	Checks communication between frontend, backend, database, and Gemini API.
Functional Testing	Verifies that all application functions work according to requirements.
UI Testing	Checks buttons, forms, menus, navigation, and page layout.
AI Output Testing	Checks whether Gemini generates relevant and creative comic content.
Performance Testing	Checks application response time and performance.
Security Testing	Checks protection of user data and API credentials.
User Acceptance Testing	Allows users to test the system and provide feedback.


3. Test Cases

Test Case	Input/Action	Expected Result

TC01	Enter a valid story idea	Story should be generated
TC02	Select a genre	Story should follow the selected genre
TC03	Enter character details	Characters should be included correctly
TC04	Click Generate	Gemini should generate comic content
TC05	Enter empty input	System should display a validation message
TC06	Generate dialogues	Relevant character dialogues should appear
TC07	Generate comic panels	Story should be divided into panels
TC08	Edit generated story	Changes should be saved correctly
TC09	Save project	Comic should be stored successfully
TC10	Gemini/API failure	Appropriate error message should be displayed
TC11	Export comic	Comic should be exported successfully
TC12	Open saved project	Previously saved content should be displayed


4. Gemini AI Testing

Special attention is given to Gemini-generated content.

The system checks whether:

The generated story matches the user's prompt.

Characters remain consistent.

Dialogues are appropriate for the characters.

Scenes follow the story sequence.

The requested number of panels is generated.

The output does not contain unnecessary or unrelated content.

The system can regenerate content when the user is not satisfied.


5. Error Handling

The application should properly handle:

Empty or invalid user input.

Internet connection problems.

Gemini API errors.

API request limits.

Database connection errors.

Unexpected AI responses.


Instead of crashing, the application should display a clear message and provide an option to retry.

6. User Acceptance Testing

A group of users can test ComicCraft-AI by creating different types of comics such as:

Superhero

Fantasy

Adventure

Comedy

Mystery

Romance


Users provide feedback about ease of use, story quality, generation speed, interface design, and overall experience.

7. Testing Result

After testing and debugging, the system should be able to:

Accept user story ideas.

Generate creative stories using Gemini.

Create characters, scenes, and dialogues.

Organize stories into comic panels.

Allow users to edit and regenerate content.

Save and retrieve comic projects.

Handle errors appropriately.


8. Final Testing Outcome

The testing phase ensures that ComicCraft-AI – Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models is reliable, user-friendly, and ready for deployment. Any errors found during testing are corrected before the final version of the application is released.
